# THE REGISTER STAYS IN. idiot.yaml is the ledger of every accusation in this
# repo and .proofs/ is the captured red-then-green of each one, which is the
# evidence that a fix was ever a fix. Peter: "leave the idiot and .proofs in the
# repo."
#
# Nothing an agent leaves behind belongs in the repo either: instructions to a
# coding assistant, its scratch notes, its handover. None of these exist here
# yet; the rules are so none ever arrive by accident.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.aider*
.mcp.json
docs/HANDOVER.md

# The global gitignore carries Python packaging's `parts/`, which matches this
# repo's part library and its tests. Nothing under either had ever been
# committed: the catalogue, the device store and nine test files lived only on
# disk. A repo .gitignore outranks the global one, so these put them back.
!src/parts/
!tests/parts/
